# Prefill20 (2026-10-17, config F): prefill-lane changes of the Mac lane, all lossless and OFF/identical unless the env says otherwise:
#  (1) STRATA_PF_CFG=<file> ("mc=6 div=512 pair=2 g=6 lag=-1"), re-read at the start of every prefill: chunk count, job size, group depth, lag, for in-server A/B without a restart (keys left out keep the env defaults).
#  (2) STRATA_PF_PAIR=N (N >= 2) makes the shared Metal job an N-chunk job (1 = the pair, as in config E): the job's fixed cost (decode of every cold expert's weights, ~37 ms for 290 experts) is paid once per N chunks.
#  (3) STRATA_PF_MIN_CHUNKS stays an env default that STRATA_PF_CFG can override.
#  (4) the packed x8 rows' device buffer gets +16 KiB and its download is rounded up to whole 16 KiB pages: no tail edge, so the shim's lazy download no longer pays a synchronous 3 ms read per layer.
# Base: Strata v0.1.41 (fb58e0dbc839) + patches/strata/0001..0021, applied in order with `git apply -p1`.

